From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:42:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gpu-compositor: the parts' picture in the frame's own job,
 from the same tree state (E2)

T-505, after two adversarial reviews of the parts on the CPU (the inspector's design E2): a frame
composed without its parts (flag 128) and posted with compose_post2/start2 (overview_ok answers 3)
carries a parts buffer and the signature of the picture the daemon holds.
- In the job, before the frame's compose: the parts' list (every fixed and sticky layer, whole
  rects), their signature (each part subtree's layers: identity, type, opacity, content flags,
  mask, visible region; inside a part its transform and clip; a colour layer's colour; an
  animation every composite; the paints under a part; the parts' sizes), the card's hold set
  (fixed and stuck layers, T-544's meaning) and a cover flag (a content leaf drawn above a part
  whose pixels meet it). When the signature is not the daemon's, the parts alone are composed on
  the band surface, packed in shelves, and read with their alpha into the buffer (a verify guard
  holds the diff baseline, the probe, the last scroll and view). Flag 2: the parts too big.
- The poll's 49 ints: the signature, the pass's bytes, the flags, the hold set.
- Review fixes: no column reads in a frame without its parts (the daemon restores what lay beneath
  them by whole rows); 0071's own-slot compensation only without the parts or with no fixed rects.
- LayerManagerComposite::JihadPrepareOnly (visible regions and effective transforms without the
  diff), CompositorOGL::JihadReadPacked (a packed read that keeps the alpha).

